<title>USA: Livingston Survey sees U.S. GDP +2.1 PCT in 1997.</title>
<headline>Livingston Survey sees U.S. GDP +2.1 PCT in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia semi-annual Livingston survey of private forecasters. 1997 GDP Q4 over Q4; 1997 CPI, PPI Dec to Dec:</p>
<p>		Q4 96   1st half 97   Full year 97    10-year avg</p>
<p>Real GDP    2.3 pct   2.0 pct	 2.1 pct	  2.4 pct</p>
<p>PPI	   N/A	 2.4 pct	 2.4 pct	  N/A</p>
<p>CPI	   N/A	 3.1 pct	 3.0 pct	  3.0 pct</p>
<p>		 Unemployment and interest rates</p>
<p>			    Dec '96	 June '97	 Dec 97</p>
<p> Unemployment Rate    5.3 pct	 5.3 pct	  5.4 pct</p>
<p> 3-month T-bill	 5.1 pct	 5.2 pct	  5.2 pct</p>
</text>
